# A result we only read the outside of says so on its own row.
#
# "decision" is in two threads: the one whose transcript is in memory, and one
# that has never been opened on this machine — for that one the search saw a
# title and a preview and nothing else. Both are worth showing; only one of
# them is evidence that the word appears in the conversation, and a list that
# renders them identically is lying about the weaker one.
#
# Opened through the state knob because Cmd+Shift+F cannot be scripted
# (afterhours_gaps.md #49).
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_XSEARCH_DEMO=decision

# The thread we hold in full: no qualifier on the row.
expect_text "needs a decision before it can go on"

# The thread we do not: marked, on the row itself.
expect_text "auto-stars — stars decision on you  (title and preview only)"
